    "statement" : "Water samples were taken at a number of locations, all data stored\n                    in one file.\n\n                    a) Cleveland Bay       CLEVELAB.WS\n\n                    Data are stored with all sites in one file.  The structure of\n                    this file is illustrated below.  Column 1 contains the date and\n                    time of the start of a measurement as a 14 digit numeric string.\n                    Column 2 represents the same date and time, but as a decimal day\n                    number, where 1.00000 represents midnight of 1 January 1993.\n                    Columns 3-6 represent the suspended sediment concentration (SSC)\n                    in mg/l.  Column 7 represents the site number.\n\n                    -------------------------------------------------\n                    YYYYMMDDhhmmss     t     mg/l mg/l mg/l mg/l Site\n                    -------------------------------------------------\n                    19930104000000   4.00000   29   29   *    *    1\n                    19930104000000   4.00000   32   38   *    *    2\n                    19930104000000   4.00000   29   29   *    *    8\n                    19930104000000   4.00000   28   31   *    *   10\n                    19930104000000   4.00000   35   47   *    *   12\n\n                    -------------------------------------------------\n                    YYYYMMDDhhmmss     t     mg/l mg/l mg/l mg/l Site\n                    -------------------------------------------------\n                    19930118000000  18.00000   28   50   *    *   13\n                    19930118000000  18.00000   32   47   *    *   15\n                    19930118000000  18.00000   38   46   *    *   19\n                    ........................................\n\n                    Site_1=146 58.85  19 13.11\n                    Site_2=146 58.34  19 11.87\n                    Site_3=146 57.51  19 10.52\n                    Site_40=146 57.01  19 08.